# Site Copy — Plain Facts Only

The website states **what the software does**. It does not argue a case, and it
does not defend design decisions. This applies to every page, card, heading and
meta tag in this repo.

## Never write

- **Negation lists.** "no Caddy, no tunnel, no openssl", "no reverse proxy",
  "no format lock-in", "no second store". If the software runs without a
  component, say what it does instead: "generates the certificate inside the
  container".
- **Defensive clauses.** Anything shaped like "X stays on", "never disables the
  guard", "is never switched off", "refuses to start rather than silently
  falling back to plaintext". These answer an objection the reader has not
  raised. If a behaviour matters, name the flag that controls it.
- **Justification tails.** "— which makes it idempotent", "so a client connects
  with no manual step", "so your AI gets smarter over time", "stop using it and
  you keep everything". State the mechanism; let the reader draw the
  conclusion.
- **Editorialising qualifiers.** "genuinely", "deliberately", "not just a
  vector DB", "not hobby projects", "reliable at scale", "maximum precision",
  "Zero noise", "spam Git", "forcing the LLM".
- **Comparative framing.** "~90% token reduction vs. agent-driven file
  reading", "10-25% higher precision". Report an unqualified measured figure or
  report nothing.
- **Claim-style headings.** "PERSISTENT MEMORY THAT COMPOUNDS",
  "ENTERPRISE-READY BY DESIGN", "ZERO CLOUD, ZERO LOCK-IN". Headings name a
  capability: "PERSISTENT MEMORY ACROSS SESSIONS", "MULTI-REPO, HOT-SWAP,
  TELEMETRY".

## Always write

- The mechanism, in one or two sentences.
- The exact configuration names that control it — `MCP_SSE_ALLOWED_HOSTS`,
  `MCP_SSE_TLS_AUTO`, `~/.flaiwheel/ca.pem`, `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS`. A reader
  should be able to act on the card without opening the README.
- Numbers only when they are real and attributable. An unsourced percentage in
  a marketing card is a fabricated claim.

## Shape

Feature card:

```
Mechanism. Configuration that controls it. Limit, if there is one.
```

## Test

Read the sentence and ask: *is this a fact about the software, or an argument
for it?* If it argues, cut everything after the mechanism.

## Keep

Deliberate brand elements are not prose: the `EVERY BUG FIXED MAKES THE NEXT
BUG CHEAPER` tagline, `THE CYCLE NEVER STOPS. KNOWLEDGE ONLY GROWS.`, the
arcade styling, and the third-party product cards under `// ALSO BY 4RCE`
(those describe other products and follow their own voice).
